Fruit Crumble
  --Genevieve Ko

Crumble:
1 1/2 c/154 g instant oats (see Tip)
3/4 c/150 g sugar
1/2 c/56 g chopped pecans or walnuts
1 tsp chai spice or ground cinnamon (see Tip)
1 tsp fine salt
1/2 c/114 g unsalted butter, at room temperature

Heat oven to 375F with a rack in the center. Mix the oats, sugar, nuts, chai spice and salt in a medium bowl. Cut the butter into cubes the size of dice and toss in. Use your fingers to smush the butter into the dry ingredients until no yellow bits remain and the blend forms clumps. Refrigerate uncovered while you prepare the fruit (or covered for up to 3 days).

Fruit:
2 lb fruit, such as berries, pears, apples, peaches, plums or a combination
1/2 c/100 g sugar
2 tbsp cornstarch or flour
1 tbsp lemon juice

If you’re using big fruit, scrub it well, then cut into 1/2" pieces, about the same size as small blackberries or big blueberries. Throw out any pits, seeds or stems. In a large bowl, mix the sugar and cornstarch. Add all the fruit, then the lemon juice and stir until well mixed. Scrape the fruit and any juices into a 9 or 10" ovenproof skillet and spread evenly. Scatter the chilled crumble mixture evenly over the fruit, breaking any large clumps into smaller pebbles. Place the skillet on a sheet pan to catch any dripping fruit juices. Bake until the fruit is bubbling, the liquid has thickened and the top is nicely browned, ~45 min. If the crumble darkens too much before the fruit mixture is thick, place a sheet of foil loosely on top. Cool for at least 15 min before serving.


Notes: can use apple pie spice blend, pumpkin pie spice blend, or baharat
